{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489217-organisations-your-sorcerer-or-psychic-could-be-in-that-aren-t-in-m20-sorcerer","id":1489217,"title":"Organisations your sorcerer or psychic could be in that aren't in M20 Sorcerer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-05T04:40:36-07:00","id":1489217,"title":"Organisations your sorcerer or psychic could be in that aren't in M20 Sorcerer","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Just a few other options that didn't get a mention in the new sorcerer book. Not an exhaustive list, just the ones I know of with a wiki article.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Division Six: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Division_Six_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Division_Six_(WOD)</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Insight Investments: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Insight_Investments\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Insight_Investments</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Piercers of the Veil: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Piercers_of_the_Veil\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Piercers_of_the_Veil</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Project Zmei: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Project_Zmei#_=_\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Project_Zmei</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Serpentines: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/The_Serpentines\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/The_Serpentines</a></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Seven Sisters: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Seven_Sisters?so=search\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Seven_Sisters</a><br /> <br /> I maybe could have added projection firms like Orpheus Group and NextWorld too. It's hinted at that they recruit psychics as well. But never spelled out directly, Orpheus mostly shied away from crossover.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T20:02:47-07:00","id":1489296,"title":"","content":"I've no idea what all is mentioned in M20 Sorcerer, but one group from Orpheus was the Midnight Star, a tabloid newspaper based specifically on the sort that were popular in the US during the 70s, 80s, and 90s. While they do/did a fair amount of celebrity and political gossip, they also did a lot of articles on cryptids (Bigfoot, Batboy, sewer alligators, etc.), UFOs, serial killers, hauntings, and so forth. While real world tabloids tended to be a bit tongue in cheek about these sort of things (to the point where the Weekly World News was just blatantly making stuff up for laughs), in the World of Darkness, the Midnight Star takes this fairly seriously, similarly to Kolcheck the Nightstalker. And like a lot of papers back then, they would hire or work with professional psychics. (Also parapsychologists, cryptozoologists, cult deprogrammers, exorcists, and other fringe types, making them a good basis for a Psychics, Hunters Hunted, or Ghostfinders campaign.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T04:13:13-07:00","id":1490696,"title":"","content":"I thought of another one, suited for Victorian Mage specifically; the Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Enlightened_Society_of_the_Weeping_Moon\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/En...e_Weeping_Moon</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:20:43-07:00","id":1491211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489217-organisations-your-sorcerer-or-psychic-could-be-in-that-aren-t-in-m20-sorcerer?p=1490696#post1490696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought of another one, suited for Victorian Mage specifically; the Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Enlightened_Society_of_the_Weeping_Moon\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/En...e_Weeping_Moon</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a good one. I also like to think that the Victorian Tremere probably had their own Golden Dawn/Weeping Moon style mystical society as a combination recruiting arm, means of societal influence, and occult studies department. Something that ended up being an odd mix of neonate and ancilea vampires, ghouls, sorcerers, dabblers, believers who don't actually have any powers, hangers on, wannabes, ladder climbers, and dupes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T20:06:52-07:00","id":1492131,"title":"","content":"I have found over the years that some of the groups from Hunter the Vigil worked as sorcerer groups, especially Ashwood Abbey, Keepers of the Source, and the Sisterhood sorority group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T14:23:42-07:00","id":1515478,"title":"","content":"Rereading some old Orpheus material I recently learned that the DEA has a Pigment Drug Enforcement Taskforce. So that's another Project Twilight related affiliation that could work for Sorcerer. Probably most specifically if your chronicle is about taking on Spectre cults in Latin America. But since some of my favorite shows involve drug cartels; that sounds like a fun, be it quite dark, game to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T04:53:06-07:00","id":1515528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489217-organisations-your-sorcerer-or-psychic-could-be-in-that-aren-t-in-m20-sorcerer?p=1491211#post1491211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a good one. I also like to think that the Victorian Tremere probably had their own Golden Dawn/Weeping Moon style mystical society as a combination recruiting arm, means of societal influence, and occult studies department. Something that ended up being an odd mix of neonate and ancilea vampires, ghouls, sorcerers, dabblers, believers who don't actually have any powers, hangers on, wannabes, ladder climbers, and dupes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really like this idea, can imagine a proxy rivalry between Tremere and Hermes sponsored Golden Dawn-esque orders, which causes The Order of Reason headaches as it promotes the Occult.<br /> <br /> Also poses an interesting possibility in a London or British Victorian Occult order (even the Order of Hermes) receiving assistance from Mithras to destabilise the Tremere and their fronts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T11:01:39-07:00","id":1515545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489217-organisations-your-sorcerer-or-psychic-could-be-in-that-aren-t-in-m20-sorcerer?p=1515528#post1515528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also poses an interesting possibility in a London or British Victorian Occult order (even the Order of Hermes) receiving assistance from Mithras to destabilise the Tremere and their fronts.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>During the Victorian and Edwardian periods, it wouldn't surprise me for Mithras to have revived the old Roman era Mithras mystery cult as an Occult order (and blood cult). Said group would likely fall apart after WW2, but would make for fun allies, rivals, or antagonists for vampires, mummies, mages, sorcerers, or mortal hunters during the Victorian or Pulp eras.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T12:34:46-07:00","id":1515549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1489217-organisations-your-sorcerer-or-psychic-could-be-in-that-aren-t-in-m20-sorcerer?p=1515545#post1515545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the Victorian and Edwardian periods, it wouldn't surprise me for Mithras to have revived the old Roman era Mithras mystery cult as an Occult order (and blood cult). Said group would likely fall apart after WW2, but would make for fun allies, rivals, or antagonists for vampires, mummies, mages, sorcerers, or mortal hunters during the Victorian or Pulp eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an excellent idea, yes very fitting which results in a three way proxy battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}